[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4572294136","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119853#issuecomment-4572294136","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119853","id":4572294136,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEIer-A","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T07:56:01Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T07:56:01Z","body":"I still think there is scarcely any good usecase for this pattern. Both links you provided mention drawbacks of it.\n\nThe boundary to the scene tree is not type safe. Obsessing over safe lines wont lead to better code. Also worth noting that inference without cast is safe but not equivalent, because it only infers `Node`.\n\nAll that being said. It's probably fine to still provide autocompletion for the cast case. As long as we draw the line there and don't go into more complex expressions (e.g. ternaries).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4572294136/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4577455462","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119853#issuecomment-4577455462","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119853","id":4577455462,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABENZtZg","user":{"login":"Copperplate","id":16230743,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjMwNzQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16230743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate","html_url":"https://github.com/Copperplate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T16:21:08Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T16:21:08Z","body":"@HolonProduction Thank you. Yes, that's very true. And you're right, using inference **WITHOUT** the cast produces \"Unsafe Method Access\" warnings, and using it **WITH** the cast breaks autocomplete for the parameter path. So perhaps then this might be one practical scenario to support, if only for the reason of continuity.\n\nHave a good weekend.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repo